language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ fifty_puzzle: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ A side show has a number of numbered dummies. Each dummy has a number on it. Choose a set of dummies to knock over so that the numbers on the dummies knocked over add up to exactly a given target sum, neither more nor less.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `fifty_puzzle.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/fifty_puzzle.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `fifty_puzzle_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py fifty_puzzle.json
$   savilerow model.eprime fifty_puzzle_1.param -run-solver

$ values_dim1: the number of dummies (derived from the data; the length of values)
given values_dim1 : int(1..)
$ values[i]: the number on dummy i, indices 1-based
given values : matrix indexed by [int(1..values_dim1)] of int
$ the target sum the knocked-over numbers must add up to exactly
given target_sum : int

$ dummies[i]: dummy i is knocked over
find dummies : matrix indexed by [int(1..values_dim1)] of bool

branching on [dummies]

such that
$ the numbers on the dummies knocked over add up to exactly the target sum
(sum i : int(1..values_dim1) . toInt(dummies[i]) * values[i]) = target_sum
